otal_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The following piece of code: https://getpsalm.org/r/1f80193969\r\n\r\n```php\r\n<?php\r\n\r\nstrtr(file_get_contents('foobar.txt'), [\r\n    'foo' => 'bar',\r\n]);\r\n```\r\n\r\nProduces the error:\r\n\r\n```\r\nERROR: InvalidArgument - 3:40 - Argument 2 of strtr expects string, array{foo:string(bar)} provided\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe actual error should be that the the first argument must have a type `string`, but `file_get_contents()` returns `string|false`. It correctly identifies that there is no matching signature, but I'm guessing due to multiple definitions of `strtr` in the call map, the actual error message ends up being misleading.","closed_by":{"login":"muglug","id":2292638,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTI2Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2292638?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug","html_url":"https://github.com/muglug","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/831/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/831/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}